WEBVTT

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:10.269
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Bank holiday or not, here we are. Can you all hear me?</v>

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:16.589
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah. Before we start, whose new car's that in the car park? Very shiny for this place.</v>

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:21.070
<v Callum Reid>Not mine. Mine's the one with more dust than paint.</v>

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:30.260
<v Fiona Doyle>Someone's doing all right, then. Also, the heating in the portakabin — honestly, it's tropical in here. Just having a moan, not reporting a job.</v>

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:34.850
<v Marcus Hale>Luxury. Normally you can see your breath on these calls.</v>

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:39.590
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before this becomes the accommodation review. What's already finished?</v>

00:00:40.289 --> 00:00:44.140
<v Priya Raman>I tested the water system yesterday and it's all fine now.</v>

00:00:45.609 --> 00:00:48.759
<v Sarah Okafor>That's complete, then, rather than something carried into today?</v>

00:00:50.969 --> 00:00:53.420
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, complete. Nothing outstanding from that test.</v>

00:00:54.759 --> 00:01:00.009
<v Hannah Price>And I already swapped the filter on the line one yesterday. That's done as well.</v>

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:03.539
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, saw that on the handover. Cheers.</v>

00:01:04.439 --> 00:01:13.189
<v Hannah Price>Only other thing from me on running conditions: saw the pressure on the stacker dip for a few minutes. It came back on its own.</v>

00:01:13.959 --> 00:01:16.760
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Sorry, did you say it's still down, or—?</v>

00:01:18.579 --> 00:01:24.879
<v Hannah Price>No, back on its own. Just an observation, not asking for a job off the back of it.</v>

00:01:25.430 --> 00:01:34.879
<v Callum Reid>Similar here. Saw the pressure on the heater box on one dip for a few minutes, then it came back on its own. Just passing that on.</v>

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:39.900
<v Marcus Hale>Right, two brief dips, neither still sitting low. Got you.</v>

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:45.640
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, observations only. We're not turning those into new actions in this meeting.</v>

00:01:46.549 --> 00:01:49.700
<v Sarah Okafor>I'll run the monthly fire alarm test this morning.</v>

00:01:50.599 --> 00:01:52.700
<v Marcus Hale>That's you doing it, boss, yeah?</v>

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:56.439
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, me. This morning.</v>

00:01:57.480 --> 00:02:04.129
<v Fiona Doyle>On the blocked stuff, I can't get to the gas valve on one until production gives us a window.</v>

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:10.689
<v Callum Reid>And there's no window agreed. I can't give you one on this call.</v>

00:02:13.069 --> 00:02:16.919
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. Still blocked, not a commitment to get at it today.</v>

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:23.500
<v Marcus Hale>Still waiting on parts for the wrapper as well. Nothing we can do until they arrive.</v>

00:02:25.139 --> 00:02:28.990
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, that's the physical work. The near-miss write-up is separate, though.</v>

00:02:30.849 --> 00:02:36.449
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. Olumide, can you write up the near miss at the wrapper after lunch? Normal priority.</v>

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:41.439
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, I'll write up the near miss at the wrapper after lunch.</v>

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:46.280
<v Sarah Okafor>Cheers. Normal priority, no need to treat the paperwork as an emergency.</v>

00:02:47.289 --> 00:02:50.090
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Understood. That's mine, separate from the parts hold.</v>

00:02:50.599 --> 00:02:55.150
<v Sarah Okafor>And the shutdown on the boiler is cancelled now. Production need it running.</v>

00:02:57.639 --> 00:03:00.090
<v Marcus Hale>Right, cancelled, not just shifted a bit.</v>

00:03:02.050 --> 00:03:06.250
<v Fiona Doyle>Good distinction. So there's no boiler shutdown going ahead under that plan.</v>

00:03:07.719 --> 00:03:08.919
<v Sarah Okafor>Correct. It's off.</v>

00:03:11.219 --> 00:03:17.169
<v Callum Reid>Yeah so, I'll update the risk assessment for work on the Gas Turbine 1, at half two.</v>

00:03:17.849 --> 00:03:20.300
<v Priya Raman>Sorry, you clipped slightly there. Half two?</v>

00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:26.300
<v Callum Reid>At half two, yeah. The risk assessment update, not the turbine work itself.</v>

00:03:26.909 --> 00:03:30.409
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Reidy. Not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:35.949
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, understood. I'll have that update at half two.</v>

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:44.000
<v Hannah Price>I'll chase the purchase order for the line 1 mould temp next week. It's fairly important.</v>

00:03:45.110 --> 00:03:50.360
<v Fiona Doyle>Next week for the chase, then? Not saying the kit will be here next week?</v>

00:03:50.759 --> 00:03:56.360
<v Hannah Price>Exactly. Chasing the purchase order, no delivery promise. Fairly important, but the chase is next week.</v>

00:03:57.599 --> 00:04:00.050
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, Pricey, that's yours for next week.</v>

00:04:01.909 --> 00:04:03.310
<v Hannah Price>Yep, I'll take it.</v>

00:04:05.710 --> 00:04:10.259
<v Fiona Doyle>And I'll inspect the pump in the pit for leaks on the 3rd.</v>

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:15.780
<v Marcus Hale>On the 3rd, right. I nearly heard that as one for today.</v>

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:24.019
<v Fiona Doyle>No, on the 3rd. Not an emergency but don't let it slip — that's how I'm treating it.</v>

00:04:25.250 --> 00:04:29.100
<v Sarah Okafor>Agreed, Fiona. The leak inspection on the 3rd is with you.</v>

00:04:29.819 --> 00:04:31.019
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, mine.</v>

00:04:32.610 --> 00:04:38.910
<v Priya Raman>Um, there's still the permit to work and isolation for the door switch on two. That needs sorting.</v>

00:04:39.589 --> 00:04:50.089
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, someone needs to sort the permit to work and isolation for the door switch on two. Not an emergency but don't let it slip. Anyone able to own that?</v>

00:04:50.709 --> 00:04:55.610
<v Priya Raman>I'm raising the gap, rather than volunteering. I can't take ownership of that package.</v>

00:04:56.540 --> 00:05:00.389
<v Olumide Adeyemi>No, I can't take the whole permit and isolation package either.</v>

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:04.759
<v Sarah Okafor>Anyone else? Sorry, thought someone was coming in there.</v>

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:10.310
<v Hannah Price>Only me moving the headset. Not an offer, sorry.</v>

00:05:12.610 --> 00:05:16.459
<v Fiona Doyle>That one's still got no owner, then. No date agreed either.</v>

00:05:17.629 --> 00:05:23.579
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. It needs doing, but nobody's taken it. Leave it explicitly unallocated, not against anyone by assumption.</v>

00:05:25.490 --> 00:05:29.689
<v Marcus Hale>Heard that. Teams makes every silence sound like someone's about to volunteer.</v>

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:32.819
<v Callum Reid>Dangerous game, breathing near your microphone.</v>

00:05:33.920 --> 00:05:35.670
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, I'll stay very still.</v>

00:05:36.240 --> 00:05:41.490
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, that's us. Agreed actions as discussed; blocked and cancelled work stays separate. Cheers, everyone.</v>
